{{!--
  Shot-pattern RESOLUTION card (CP2020 p.108) — posted for a corridor the shooter already aimed, once
  the shot has finished being presented, in place of resolving it unattended. Rendered via
  renderChatCard with
  { weaponName, band, widthM, dmgFormula, shells, multiShell, templateId,
    rows: [{ name, status }], anyRows }.
  `status` arrives PRE-LOCALIZED from JS (in pattern / behind cover), so the row stays one declarative
  shape rather than branching per figure. Rows are DIVs for the same reason spread-result.hbs uses
  them: core's layered `ul` styling wins over a module rule on this build, and a chat card wants no
  markers.

  The cp-confirm-spread-zone button + data-template-id are verbatim from spread-confirm.hbs — one
  dispatch (damage-hooks.js registerDamageHooks) resolves either card, relays to the active GM, and
  locks the card against a second press. i18n via CPLocal; triple-stash where the string carries <b>.
--}}
<div class="cyberpunk save-prompt">
  <h3>{{CPLocal "SpreadConfirmTitle" weapon=weaponName}}</h3>
  <div class="save-info">
    <span>{{{CPLocal "SpreadConfirmSummary" band=band width=widthM dmg=dmgFormula}}}</span><br>
    {{#if multiShell}}
      <span>{{{CPLocal "SpreadConfirmShells" shells=shells dmg=dmgFormula}}}</span><br>
    {{/if}}
    <div class="cp-spread-resolve-list">
      {{#if anyRows}}
        {{#each rows}}
          <div class="cp-spread-resolve-row">{{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveRow" name=this.name status=this.status}}}</div>
        {{/each}}
      {{else}}
        <div class="cp-spread-resolve-row">{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveNobody"}}</div>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    <span class="save-note">{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveBasis"}}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="save-buttons">
    <button class="cp-confirm-spread-zone" data-template-id="{{templateId}}">{{CPLocal "SpreadResolveBtn"}}</button>
  </div>
</div>
